      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being fundamentally broken is a heavy burden, but it's also a sign that you recognize the gravity of what happened. The guilt you feel is proof that you have a conscience, which is a trait of a good person, even if your actions were catastrophic. Instead of letting this mistake define your entire existence, consider what small, tangible steps you can take now to begin addressing the damage, even if it feels impossible.",
      "source": "target",
